cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Symphysis in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Symphysis: Config-Driven Agent Panels for Expert-Elicitation Surveys"
abstract: >-
  A config-driven engine for running structured expert-elicitation surveys
  (Best-Worst Method, Analytic Hierarchy Process, and multi-level
  hierarchical variants) against a panel of real, individually configured
  AI agents, alongside or in place of a human panel. Every agent is
  defined by a portable, self-certifying Agent Card (did:key identity,
  role, model, RAG corpus, permissions, guardrails), so an identical panel
  can be respawned anywhere from one JSON file per agent.
